## AIM

- The purpose of this Qualification Standard (QS) is to describe in operational terms, the required outcome of individual training and education (IT&E) for Pte Cyber Operators.

## PREREQUISITES

- This QS was developed with the intent that the candidates will meet the following prerequisites prior to being course loaded:

- English language profile of BBB; and

- Basic Military Qualification (BMQ) (AINT).

- The loading authority must ensure that candidates meet those prerequisites. 

## BACKGROUND

- This document contains the following Performance Objectives (POs) that the member shall achieve to meet the requirements of this qualification:

| **PO** | **PO Title** |
| --- | --- |
| 001 | Develop scripts for simple task automation |
| 002 | Maintain hardware environment |
| 003 | Maintain software environment |
| 004 | Characterize a network |
| 005 | Deploy Active Directory environment |
| 006 | Set up log and traffic collection |
| 007 | Configure security appliances |
| 008 | Conduct network discovery |
| 009 | Inform on cyber threats |
| 010 | Identify malicious behaviour in network traffic |
| 011 | Triage artifacts |
| 012 | Identify malicious behaviour in host logs |
| 013 | Extract artifacts for digital forensic analysis |
| 014 | Investigate cyber incident |
| 015 | Apply cyber security orders and directives |

## USE OF QUALIFICATION STANDARD

- This QS shall be used by the IT&E establishment to design, develop, conduct, and evaluate the training program.

- This QS will also be used by MPGTG Standards in support of validation.

- The qualification code/title supported by the POs:

| **Qualification Code** | **National Qualification Title** |
| --- | --- |
| Temp 99 | Rank Qualification Cyber Operator Private |

	

