##  PO 001 Develop Scripts for Simple Task Automation

- Performance: Develop Scripts for Simple Task Automation.

- Conditions:

- given:

- references; and

- supervision;

- denied: nil; and

- environment: day or night within a technical environment.

- Standard: The Pte Cyber Operator shall, IAW C5, develop scripts for simple task automation by:

- (FT0280) developing software tools to include:

- building a basic unconditional program; and

- building a script.

- Remarks:

- the scope of the PO is for the Pte RQ Cyber Operator to create simple scripts to conduct basic task automation;

- training should be in line with a first-year post-secondary level introduction to programming course; and

- no access to Artificial Intelligence (AI)/assistance to ensure that the member has foundational comprehension of programming concepts.

## PO 002 Maintain Hardware Environment

- Performance: Maintain hardware environment.

- Conditions:

- given:

- hardware;

- references; and

- supervision;

- denied: nil; and

- environment: day or night within a technical environment.

- Standard: The Pte Cyber Operator shall, IAW ref C1, maintain hardware environment by:

- (FT0010) installing hardware;

- (FT0030) configuring hardware;

- verifying functionality of hardware to include:

- testing functionality of hardware; and

- (FT0110) troubleshooting toolset hardware deficiencies; and

- (FT0020) removing hardware.

- Remarks: Nil.

## PO 003 Maintain Software Environment

- Performance: Maintain software environment. 

- Conditions:

- given:

- references; and

- supervision;

- denied: nil; and

- environment: day or night within a technical environment.

- Standard: The Pte Cyber Operator shall, IAW refs C1 and C17, maintain software environment by:

- deploying Operating Systems (OS) to include:

- Windows; and

- Linux;

- configuring OS;

- (FT0040) installing software;

- (FT0050) removing software;

- (FT0060) configuring software; and

- (FT0080) troubleshooting toolset software deficiencies.

- Remarks: Nil.

## PO 004 Characterize a Network

- Performance: Characterize a network.

- Conditions:

- given:

- references; and

- supervision;

- denied: nil; and

- environment: day or night, within a technical environment.

- Standard: The Pte Cyber Operator shall, IAW ref C3, characterize a network by:

- identifying routing and subnetting;

- identifying network services; and

- identifying additional network functionality.

- Remarks: Nil.

## PO 005 Deploy Active Directory Environment

- Performance: Deploy Active Directory environment.

- Conditions:

- given:

- licenses;

- references; and

- supervision;

- denied: nil; and

- environment: day or night within a technical environment.

- Standard: The Pte Cyber Operator shall, IAW ref C7, deploy Active Directory (AD) environment by:

- designing a Windows identity infrastructure;

- managing an AD; and

- managing AD tasks with PowerShell.

- Remarks: Nil.

## PO 006 Set up Log and Traffic Collection

- Performance: Set up log and traffic collection.

- Conditions:

- given:

- references; and

- supervision;

- denied: nil; and

- environment: day or night, within a technical environment.

- Standard: The Pte Cyber Operator shall, IAW refs C3, C4, C8 set up log and traffic collection by:

- (ET0051) deploying endpoint agents to include:

- installing endpoint agents;

- configuring audit logs; and

- removing endpoint agents;

- (ET0052) deploying taps to include:

- installing taps; and

- configuring taps;

- (ET0060) collecting network traffic and logs to include:

- log forwarding; 

- (ET0061) collecting metadata from network traffic; and

- (ET0062) collecting metadata from host logs;

- (ET0053) validating log and traffic collection.

- Remarks: Nil.

## PO 007 Configure Security Appliances

- Performance: Configure security appliances.

- Conditions:

- given:

- references; and

- supervision;

- denied: nil; and

- environment: day or night, within a technical environment.

- Standard: The Pte Cyber Operator shall, IAW refs C2, C8, C10, and C20 - C35, configure security appliances by:

- deploying security appliances to include:

- firewall;

- Host-based Intrusion Detection System (HIDS); and

- Network-based Intrusion Detection System (NIDS)/Intrusion Prevention System (IPS); and

- creating protocol specific rules for security appliances to include:

- (FT0160) developing network sensor rule;

- creating basic rules for security appliances; 

- (FT0130) loading network sensor rules to sensors; and

- (FT0180) testing network sensor rule functionality.

- Remarks: Nil.

## PO 008 Conduct Network Discovery

- Performance: Conduct network discovery.

- Conditions:

- given:

- references; and

- supervision;

- denied: nil;

- environment: day or night within a technical environment.

- Standard: The Pte Cyber Operator shall, IAW references C1-C3, C4, C8, C17, C36 - C38, and D26 - D30, conduct network discovery by:

- characterizing infrastructure to include:

- identifying key infrastructure;

- identifying endpoints to include:

- (BT0541) attributing software behaviour to a particular OS; 

- (BT0411) identifying operating systems based on network traffic; and

- (BT0410) identifying device applications;

- (ET0100) determining location of physical network asset; and

- (ET0090) developing logical network map;

- characterizing digital identity behaviour to include:

- identifying digital identity types on the network; 

- identifying users’ actions; and

- (GT0070) characterizing network traffic to establish normal patterns; and

- enumerating a network to include:

- identifying endpoints;

- conducting different types of network scans; 

- (ET0090) developing logical network map; and

-  (ET0080) scanning for vulnerabilities.

- Remarks: The task GT0080 “Analyze network traffic” is not reflected specifically in one area of the PO. 

## PO 009 Inform on Cyber Threats

- Performance: Inform on cyber threats.

- Conditions:

- given:

- analyst notes;

- data of the incident;

- intelligence reports;

- reporting template;

- references; and

- supervision;

- denied: nil; and

- environment: day or night within a technical environment.

- Standard: The Pte Cyber Operator shall, IAW refs B1 and C2, (BT0220) inform on cyber threats by:

- (CT0160) advising chain of command (CoC) on current cyber threat by:

- (CT0260) preparing cyber tactical briefings IAW reference B1 to include:

- collecting technical details / notes to include:

- analyst notes;

- intelligence reports; and

- Common Vulnerabilities and Exploits (CVE) data;

- reconstructing malicious activity to include:

- confirming incident data;

- analyzing incident data; and

- (BT0515) producing an activity timeline;

- compiling future actions to include:

- mitigations; and 

- recovery;

- (BT0300) advising on cyber defence enhancement by providing a briefing to the CoC; and

- producing a technical report by:

- collecting technical details / notes to include:

- analyst notes;

- intelligence reports; and

- CVE data;

- reconstructing malicious activity to include:

- confirming incident data;

- analyzing incident data; and

- (BT0515) producing an activity timeline;

- (CT0050) initiating technical report to include:

-  collating relevant data;

- (CT0200) recommending cyber incident recovery measures;

- (BT0300) advising cyber defence enhancements;

- submitting the report to include:

- producing an executive summary; and

- (CT0282) reporting on tactics, techniques, and procedures (TTPs) of malicious activity; and

- (CT0060) updating technical report.

- Remarks: Advise CoC section refers to direct supervisor and informing at the section level.

## PO 010 Identify Malicious Behaviour in Network Traffic

- Performance: Identify malicious behaviour in network traffic.

- Conditions:

- given:

- network incident data;

- reporting template;

- references; and

- supervision;

- denied: nil; and

- environment: day or night within a technical environment.

- Standard: The Pte Cyber Operator shall, IAW refs C2, C8, C9, and D1 - D13, (BT0421) identify malicious behaviour in network traffic by:

- identifying anomalies in network traffic;

- (CT0281) identifying TTPs of malicious activity;

- (BT0542) identifying indicators of cyber activity;

- identifying related events in network logs;

- identifying related Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)/artifacts for extraction;

- (GT0110) analyzing anomalies in network traffic using metadata; 

- (BT0420) reconstructing a malicious activity; and

- (BT0515) producing an activity timeline.

- Remarks:

- the task BT0370 “Identify network mapping and operating system (OS) fingerprinting activities” is not necessary to state but will be included as a learning objective in the TP;

- the tasks GT0080 “Analyze network traffic” and CT0130 “Document analysis notes” are encompassing tasks that span across the entire PO; 

- this PO falls under the task “confirm malicious activity” in PO Investigate Cyber Incident. The Pte Cyber Operator is expected to inspect network traffic and identify adversary actions semi-independently; 

- identifying TTPs does not include attribution. It is identifying the common name for a technique (ex -brute force, port scan) and its purpose in the event; and

-  “identifying anomalies in network traffic” in this PO does not entail being able to take network traffic and find anomalous behaviour without any indicators. The students should have some generic indicator (Adversary TTP Ex: Adversary leverages DNS/Phishing/Brute Force in their attacks) to scope where they conduct anomaly analysis.

## PO 011 Triage Artifacts

- Performance: Triage artifacts.

- Conditions:

- given:

- artifacts;

- reporting template;

- references; and

- supervision;

- denied: nil; and

- environment: day or night within a technical environment.

- Standard: The Pte Cyber Operator shall, IAW refs C10, C12, C15, and D14 - D17, (BT0400) triage artifacts by:

- (FT0345) preparing an analysis environment by (GT0400) creating synthetic environment;

- (GT0380) determining the key characteristics of malicious software;

- (GT0410) analyzing malicious software to include:

- (GT0370) conducting basic static analysis;

- (GT0390) conducting basic dynamic analysis;

- (GT0460) reverse engineering obfuscated software to include:

- (GT0492) identifying adversary use of anti-forensics techniques; and

- (GT0491) identifying adversary attempts to hide malicious content and behaviour; and

- (GT0520) compiling technical intelligence from analyzed malicious software.

- Remarks:

- the task CT0130 “Document analysis notes” is encompassing task that span across the entire PO;

- the member should be able to recognize if the artifact is benign, a commonly known malicious artifact (ex: mimikatz, CobaltStrike, etc.), exhibiting clear malicious behaviour (behaviours and IoCs are identified; Ex: keyloggers, droppers, etc.), or requires further analysis by a reverse engineering team;

- the member is expected to de-obfuscate common encoding methods such as base64, URL encoding, XOR, ROT-N, etc.;

- should identify that artifacts are packed/encrypted, but not expected to defeat the technique unless explicitly taught;

- the member is expected to identify behaviours/IoCs/defeat common encoding methods when encountering basic scripting in any programming language (Ex: PowerShell, Python, JavaScript, Bash, etc.).

## PO 012 Identify Malicious Behaviour in Host Logs

- Performance: Identify malicious behaviour in host logs.

- Conditions:

- given:

- host incident data;

- reporting template;

- references; and

- supervision.

- denied: nil; and

- environment: day or night within a technical environment.

- Standard: The Pte Cyber Operator shall, IAW refs C13, D3, and D18 - D24, (BT0422) identify malicious behaviour in host logs by:

- identifying anomalies in host logs;

- (CT0281) identifying TTPs of malicious activity IAW D1;

- identifying related events in host logs;

- identifying related Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)/artifacts for extraction;

- (BT0420) reconstructing a malicious activity; and

- (BT0515) producing an activity timeline.

- Remarks:

- the tasks GT0081 “analyze host logs” and CT0130 “document analysis notes” are encompassing tasks that span across the entire PO; and

- identifying TTPs does not include attribution. It is identifying the common name for a technique (ex: brute force, port scan) and its purpose in the event. 

## PO 013 Extract Artifacts for Digital Forensics Analysis

- Performance: Extract artifacts for digital forensics analysis.

- Conditions:

- given:

- digital media for forensic imaging;

- references; and

- supervision;

- denied: nil; and

- environment: day or night within a technical environment.

- Standard: The Pte Cyber Operator shall, IAW refs C14 - C17, (BT0450) extract artifacts for digital forensics analysis by:

- (ET0020) safeguarding cyber forensic evidence;

- (BT0470) documenting original condition of digital forensic artifacts;

- (BT0440) cloning digital media for forensics;

- (ET0075) conducting live memory acquisition;

- (ET0050) collecting artifact; and

- (BT0430) recovering artifacts for digital forensics analysis to include:

- (BT0435) Identify artifacts for digital forensics analysis;

- (GT0510) extracting malicious artifacts from other digital media;

- extracting deleted artifacts; and

- (BT0540) attributing a forensic artifact to a particular operating system.

- Remarks: Extracting artifacts for this PO, refers to dead disks (computer systems) not live artifacts from network/host investigations.

## PO 014 Investigate Cyber Incident

- Performance: Investigate cyber incident.

- Conditions:

- given:

- incident data;

- reporting template;

- references; and

- supervision;

- denied: nil; and

- environment: day or night within a technical environment.

- Standard: The Pte Cyber Operator shall, IAW refs C15 and C16, (BT0352) investigate cyber incidents by:

- identifying a cyber incident by:

- identifying data sources;

- (BT0330) triaging indicators of events; and

- (GT0250) analyzing security alerts;

- confirming malicious activity to include:

- identifying malicious behaviour; 

- (BT0542) identifying indicators of cyber activity

- (BT0362) extracting artifacts;

- extracting IoCs;

- (BT0361) extracting network indicators;

- (GT0150) determining adversary TTPs; and

- (GT0180) evaluating all source cyber threat information;

- determining impact of incident to include:

- (BT0515) producing an activity timeline;

- (GT0180) evaluating all source cyber threat information;

- (BT0560) researching real time open-source cyber events for Indications and Warnings (I&W) IAW reference C14;

- (GT0280) analyzing all source Indications & Warnings (I&W) of cyber events and incidents;

- identifying affected resources; and

- (GT0040) identifying means of compromise; and

- producing a complete technical report.

- Remarks: 

- the tasks BT0350 “monitor network sensors for cyber events” and CT0130 “Document analysis notes” are encompassing tasks that span across the entire PO; and 

- BT0380 “validate intrusion detection system (IDS) alerts against network traffic" is similar to para 3.b. in that validating IDS alerts also confirms malicious activity, however, “confirming malicious activity” better scopes the task.

## PO 015 Apply Cyber Security Orders and Directives

- Performance: Apply cyber security orders and directives.

- Conditions:

- given:

- references; and

- supervision;

- denied: nil; and

- environment: day or night within a technical environment.

- Standard: The Pte Cyber Operator shall, IAW ref A02, (AT0005) apply cyber security orders and directives to include:

- handling classified material IAW reference A02; and

- verifying authority to conduct network collection to include:

- confirming rules of engagement (ROE);

- confirming authorized tools; and

- validating IP ranges and targets.

- Remarks:

- the topics are to be taught as it uniquely applies to cyber operators, not as generic policy; and

- the member is expected to understand that there are limitations on open source researching as they are handling classified information.

